{"step_index":271,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:29:36Z","content":"I can see the `mcpOAuth` section for NexLev — but the `accessToken` is empty and `expiresAt` is 0. This means Claude Code CLI has the OAuth config registered but **never completed the authentication** (the browser approval step was never done successfully in Claude Code).\n\nThe token from Claude.ai web is stored on Anthropic's servers, not locally.\n\nHere's the **bottom line truth**: NexLev's own server told us:\n\n> \"Provide either: 1) OAuth Bearer token, or 2) API key (Bearer nlv_...)\"\n\n**There are exactly 2 paths to make this work:**\n\n### Path 1: API Key (30 seconds — RECOMMENDED)\n1. Go to your NexLev dashboard → click **\"NexLev API\"** in sidebar\n2. Copy the key (starts with `nlv_`)\n3. Paste it here → Done forever\n\n### Path 2: OAuth via Claude Code CLI (2 minutes)\n1. Open PowerShell\n2. Type `claude` → Enter\n3. Type `/mcp` → Enter  \n4. Select `nexlev` → press Enter\n5. Select `Authenticate` → press Enter\n6. Browser opens → log in → approve\n7. Come back here\n\n**Which one do you want to do?** Both take under 2 minutes. I literally cannot bypass authentication — NexLev's server blocks unauthenticated requests. Even Claude.ai had to authenticate (it just did it automatically for you)."}
